            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0522" n="442" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/124: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-21T17:00:00-03:00">October 21, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 21—3:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>115. German Legation [<hi rendition="#italic">Minister</hi>] informs me that his
                    Consul at Bahia reports the arrival at that port of the British cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Delhi</hi>. The Minister states that he has requested
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Karlsruhe</hi> to stop at Bahia and has instructed
                    it to get in touch with the Commander of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pensacola</hi>. The American Naval Mission in Brazil hopes to be able to
                    get in touch with the <hi rendition="#italic">Pensacola</hi> by radio this
                    evening.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
